---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Apryse DOCX Editor: Edit Word Documents in the Browser"
  description="The Apryse DOCX Editor creates and edits DOCX documents in the browser without MS Office or server-side dependencies. Andrey Safonov led it from zero to one, reaching a $3M pipeline in its first quarter."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Portfolio', path: '/portfolio' }, { name: 'DOCX Editor', path: '/portfolio/docx-product' }]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-14 sm:px-6">
    <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-medium text-accent">Portfolio · Apryse · 0→1</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">DOCX Editor</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      An embeddable web editor that creates and edits DOCX files entirely client-side, with no MS Office and no server.
      It's a zero-to-one product I built with 2 product designers and 2 scrum teams (one frontend, one backend). It built a $3M pipeline in its first quarter.
    </p>
    <img src="/cases/docx-editor.png" alt="DOCX Editor screenshot" class="mt-8 w-full rounded-2xl border border-line" />
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="https://apryse.com/blog/webviewer/docx-editor-release" class="rounded-lg bg-accent px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-accent-ink">Launch blog ↗</a>
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3VY1GMyL0AA" class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium">Watch the demo ↗</a>
      <a href="/portfolio" class="rounded-lg px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-muted">← Back to portfolio</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
